WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.660
Angle a flat mirror in sunshine.

2
00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:05.330
It throws a bright patch onto a wall.

3
00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:09.540
However you angle it, that patch
never becomes a burning spot.

4
00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:13.350
Now curve the mirror into a
dish and point it at the Sun.

5
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.140
The light can gather into a burning spot.

6
00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:17.460
Same sunlight.

7
00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:21.040
Why can the dish do what
the flat mirror never can?

8
00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:24.260
In this mission, you'll name
the parts of a curved mirror,

9
00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:27.310
and trace rays off it with
the law of reflection.

10
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.250
Then you'll sort real
images from virtual ones,

11
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.400
and find out which kind
a screen can catch.

12
00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:37.120
Your mission: explain why a
dish-shaped mirror can do it,

13
00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.920
and a flat one never can.
